SUMMARY:2026 Philosophy Undergraduate Orientation and Welcome Event
DESCRIPTION:Philosophy Undergraduates\, comes join us for an introduction to the Department of Philosophy at U of T’s St. George campus. Highlights of the event include \n-Words of welcome and brief overview of the program from Mike Miller\, the Undergraduate Chair\n-A quick survey of the department’s offerings with Profs. Monica Ding\, Andrew Franklin-Hall\, Stephen Menn and David Rattray\n-Introductions from members of the Philosophy Course Union (PCU)\, the department’s undergraduate student association\, giving a sneak peek of events in the year to come\n-Information about other philosophy student groups like Philosophers for Humanity and Noesis (UofT’s Undergraduate Journal of Philosophy)\n-And an introduction session about the PHL1 program \nA short reception will follow where you’ll have a chance to meet some of the faculty and your fellow undergraduates! Come with all your questions! \nIf you are interested in attending\, please RSVP here: 2026 Orientation RSVP
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/2026-philosophy-undergraduate-orientation-and-welcome-event/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building 100
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026-Student-Orientation-v2.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Eric Correia":MAILTO:eric.correia@utoronto.ca
