SUMMARY:Global Philosophy Research Interest Group Talk (Daniel Nolan\, UC Santa Cruz)
DESCRIPTION:The Global Philosophy Research Interest Group is delighted to welcome as guest speaker Daniel Nolan\, a professor in the Department of Philosophy at the University of California\, Santa Cruz. He specializes in metaphysics\, especially hyperintensionality and the use of impossible worlds to resolve metaphysical problems. Daniel has additional interests in possible worlds\, dispositions\, states of affairs\, universals and particulars\, parts and wholes\, time and space\, the metaphysics of vagueness\, and methodology in metaphysics. \nTalk Title\nTBA \nTalk Abstract\nTBA
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/global-philosophy-research-interest-group-talk-daniel-nolan-uc-santa-cruz/
